From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 23:59:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] dma-mapping: admit upstream hint for noncontiguous memory

Test21 safely stopped before hardware because dma_alloc_noncontiguous()
rejects every attribute except DMA_ATTR_ALLOC_SINGLE_PAGES. The IRIS1 VB2
queue passed DMA_ATTR_IOMMU_USE_UPSTREAM_HINT, so the public wrapper warned
and returned NULL before iommu-dma could create the streaming mapping.

Admit the upstream attribute in this allocator. The IOMMU implementation
already translates it to IOMMU_USE_UPSTREAM_HINT and selects MAIR 0xf4.
Other unsupported attributes remain rejected.

Signed-off-by: Codex <codex@openai.com>
---
diff --git a/kernel/dma/mapping.c b/kernel/dma/mapping.c
index e6b07f160d20..a5f906cb4707 100644
--- a/kernel/dma/mapping.c
+++ b/kernel/dma/mapping.c
@@ -802,7 +802,8 @@ struct sg_table *dma_alloc_noncontiguous(struct device *dev, size_t size,
 {
 	struct sg_table *sgt;
 
-	if (WARN_ON_ONCE(attrs & ~DMA_ATTR_ALLOC_SINGLE_PAGES))
+	if (WARN_ON_ONCE(attrs & ~(DMA_ATTR_ALLOC_SINGLE_PAGES |
+				   DMA_ATTR_IOMMU_USE_UPSTREAM_HINT)))
 		return NULL;
 	if (WARN_ON_ONCE(gfp & __GFP_COMP))
 		return NULL;
